        "description": "<div id=\"link_wrapped_content\">\n<body><section class=\"wp-block-bigbite-multi-title\"><div class=\"container\"></div></section>\n\n\n\n<p>A mobile phone battery stores enormous amounts of energy in a very small space. As long as everything is working properly, we don\u2019t notice anything. But a technical defect or incorrect handling can trigger a chain reaction \u2014 known as thermal runaway. This causes the battery to fuel itself with energy until it bursts into flames or ruptures under intense pressure. What makes this particularly dangerous is that battery fires often start silently and produce extremely toxic fumes that can attack the lungs and nervous system. This can even happen with a <a href=\"https://www.pcwelt.de/article/2210854/akku-explodiert-beim-laden-fotos-der-zerstoerung.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">cordless vacuum cleaner</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading toc\" id=\"these-charging-errors-can-set-your-home-on-fire\">These charging errors can set your home on fire",
